<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<task id="244" project="customer-provisioning-orchestration-r1">
  <metadata>
    <title>Keyless customer-stamp resources in Bicep (owner D13, plan G16) — disable local/key auth on AI Search, OpenAI, Document Intelligence, Service Bus and Storage; grant the L2 identity its Search roles; drop the secret-bearing outputs</title>
    <phase>Model 1 dedicated-stamp remediation — plan §7 T244 (owner decision D13 keyless stamps, gap G16; hard prerequisite of T186 per D22)</phase>
    <gate>startable after PR #1311 merges (T243 ✅, T242 ✅)</gate>
    <status>completed</status>
    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Auth change on every customer-stamp resource (tag auth) deployed by H2a, plus L2 RBAC, a legacy script and tests; failure mode is every stamp service call returning 401/403.</rigor-reason>
    <model-tier>sonnet</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Fully specified Bicep property changes and output removals on an existing template; the risk is a missed consumer of a key or connection string, which the steps make an explicit inventory.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>high</effort>
    <parallel-group>none</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <parallel-reason>customer.bicep / customer.json are shared by every stamp task; touches .claude/CHANGELOG.md if a constraint/pattern changes (main-session-only)</parallel-reason>
    <tags>bicep, auth, provisioning, ai-search, openai, document-intelligence, service-bus, storage, rbac, model1-dedicated, testing</tags>
    <deps>243, 242</deps>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Make a new customer stamp keyless: every stamp resource that supports it rejects key/local auth, the identities that
    need data-plane access hold the right roles, and the template stops emitting secrets.
  </prompt>

  <role>
    SPAARKE platform developer (Bicep, Azure RBAC, PowerShell provisioning scripts, the L2 control plane). Follow ADR-028
    and the provisioning constraints strictly.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A stamp deployed from `customer.bicep` has local/key auth disabled on AI Search, Azure OpenAI, Document Intelligence and
    Service Bus, and shared-key access disabled on Storage; the BFF runtime UAMI (already granted) and the L2 control-plane
    UAMI (new: Search Service Contributor + Search Index Data Contributor, for H2b index creation) reach their services
    through Entra; no module or template output carries a key or a connection string with a key.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      Owner D13 (2026-09-30): keyless customer stamps, full ADR-028 compliance; local auth disabled where Azure allows it.
      D22: T244 is a hard prerequisite of T186 (T243 switched the stamp AI platform on, which exposes AI Search MI 403 —
      plan G16 — because `modules/ai-search.bicep` sets no `authOptions`/`disableLocalAuth`, so the service is keys-only
      while H4b forces the BFF onto MI with `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`).
      State read 2026-10-06:
      - No `disableLocalAuth` on `modules/ai-search.bicep`, `openai.bicep`, `doc-intelligence.bicep`, `service-bus.bicep`;
        `storage-account.bicep` has `param disableSharedKeyAccess bool = false` (`allowSharedKeyAccess: !disableSharedKeyAccess`)
        and `customer.bicep` does not set it.
      - Key outputs still exist: `ai-search.bicep` `searchServiceAdminKey` (:82) + `searchServiceQueryKey` (:84);
        `openai.bicep` `openAiKey` (:183); `service-bus.bicep` `serviceBusConnectionString` (:61, listKeys);
        `storage-account.bicep` `connectionString` (:193, AccountKey unless shared key disabled). `customer.bicep`
        re-exports `storageConnectionString` (:793) and `serviceBusConnectionString` (:799).
      - Only `customer.bicep` calls these five modules (platform.bicep / platform-controlplane.bicep do not).
      - The only consumer of the two customer outputs found is legacy `scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1:510,514`.
      - The BFF runtime UAMI already holds Service Bus Data Sender/Receiver and Search Index Data Contributor + Search
        Service Contributor (`modules/bff-runtime-rbac.bicep`, A36/A37); the stamp BFF reaches Service Bus by
        `ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace` (MI). The L2 UAMI holds only Website Contributor on the BFF
        (`modules/customer-l2-bff-rbac.bicep`), so H2b (`H2bAiSearchIndexHandler`, DefaultAzureCredential) has no Search role.
      - `scripts/ai-search/Deploy-AllIndexes.ps1` already has an AAD-token path (:372-454) used when the BFF has
        `AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled=true`; its admin-key path remains for the shared dev env.
      - `modules/content-safety.bicep` (`disableLocalAuth: false`, `contentSafetyKey` output) is T246's scope.
      - T243 note (plan T244 row): on any stamp provisioned before T243, delete the `DocumentIntelligence__DocIntelKey`
        app setting before disabling Doc Intel local auth — a leftover key setting wins over MI. None exists today.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/ai-search.bicep (authOptions / disableLocalAuth; key outputs :82, :84)</file>
      <file>infrastructure/bicep/modules/openai.bicep (disableLocalAuth; `openAiKey` :183)</file>
