  <constraints>
    <constraint source="plan T244 (scope)">
      Customer-stamp templates only. Do NOT change shared dev/demo resources, the BFF's key fallbacks, Content Safety (T246),
      Redis (T242, already Entra-only) or Cosmos. No live Azure change in this task — the first stamp deploy (T186) proves it,
      and T230 makes one real MI call per service.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="owner D13">
      Disable local auth where Azure allows it: AI Search `disableLocalAuth: true` (with no `authOptions`, which Azure requires
      when local auth is disabled); OpenAI, Document Intelligence and Service Bus `disableLocalAuth: true`; Storage
      `allowSharedKeyAccess: false` via `disableSharedKeyAccess: true` from `customer.bicep`. If a property is rejected for
      the pinned API version, raise the API version rather than dropping the setting, and say so in the notes.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-028 / provisioning.md">
      No key or keyed connection string in any module or template output. Remove the outputs rather than suppressing the
      linter. If a module output must stay for a non-stamp caller, there is none today (only customer.bicep calls them) —
      re-check before deleting.
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="L2 RBAC">
      Grant the L2 UAMI (`controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId`) Search Service Contributor (7ca78c08-252a-4471-8644-bb5ff32d4ba0) and
      Search Index Data Contributor (8ebe5a00-799e-43f5-93ac-243d3dce84a7) on the stamp's AI Search service, scoped to the
      service, principalType ServicePrincipal, skipped when the principal id is empty — by extending
      `customer-l2-bff-rbac.bicep` (rename the module only if the name becomes misleading; §11: extend, do not add a module
      unless extension is impossible, and say why).
    </constraint>
    <constraint source="legacy script">
      `Provision-Customer.ps1` must not read the removed outputs. Replace them with keyless values it can use (endpoint /
      namespace) or remove the dependent lines, and keep its Pester tests passing.
    </constraint>
  </constraints>

  <escalation>
    <trigger>A consumer other than `Provision-Customer.ps1` reads a removed output, a storage account key, a Service Bus SAS rule or an OpenAI/Search key (H13 probe, sidecar, Event Grid dead-letter, Function, script, test) → STOP and report it before removing.</trigger>
    <trigger>Any stamp component (BFF, Worker, sidecar, H2b, H13) still authenticates to one of the five services with a key rather than an identity → STOP and report; do not disable local auth on that service.</trigger>
    <trigger>A required property is unsupported for the resource SKU/kind the stamp deploys (e.g. Service Bus tier, OpenAI kind) → STOP and report the options.</trigger>
  </escalation>

  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Inventory: grep every consumer of the five modules' key/connection-string outputs, `listKeys`/`listAdminKeys`, `AccountKey`, `SharedAccessKey`, and every stamp component's credential for each service; record the table in the notes (escalation triggers 1–2).</step>
    <step order="2">Modules: set local-auth off (constraint D13); remove the key outputs (`searchServiceAdminKey`, `searchServiceQueryKey`, `openAiKey`, `serviceBusConnectionString`, storage `connectionString`); remove the Service Bus send/listen SAS rule if nothing else uses it. Update descriptions that promise keys.</step>
    <step order="3">`customer.bicep`: pass `disableSharedKeyAccess: true` to storage; drop the `storageConnectionString` / `serviceBusConnectionString` outputs; extend `customer-l2-bff-rbac.bicep` with the two Search roles for the L2 UAMI and pass the search service name. Recompile `customer.json` (`--outfile`).</step>
    <step order="4">`Provision-Customer.ps1`: stop reading the removed outputs (constraint "legacy script").</step>
    <step order="5">Tests: update/extend whatever pins the customer template shape (outputs, role assignments, properties) so it asserts local auth off on all five services, no key outputs, and the two L2 Search roles; Pester for `Provision-Customer.ps1` if it covers those lines.</step>
    <step order="6">Docs: resource inventory, customer deployment guide and any constraint/pattern that says stamps carry keys or SAS connection strings; plan §7 T244 + G16; CHANGELOG if `.claude` changes.</step>
    <step order="7">Verify (`az bicep build`, lint clean, `customer.json` = fresh compile, `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS, ControlPlane.Tests, Pester) + Step 9.5 + close (POML notes, TASK-INDEX, plan, current-task, drift check) + commit + push.</step>
  </steps>

  <outputs>
    <output type="file-modified">modules/ai-search.bicep, openai.bicep, doc-intelligence.bicep, service-bus.bicep, storage-account.bicep, customer-l2-bff-rbac.bicep; customer.bicep + customer.json; scripts/Provision-Customer.ps1; tests pinning the template; docs</output>
  </outputs>

  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">Compiled `customer.json` has `disableLocalAuth: true` on the AI Search, OpenAI, Document Intelligence and Service Bus resources and `allowSharedKeyAccess: false` on the stamp storage account; AI Search has no `authOptions`.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No `listKeys`, `listAdminKeys`, `listQueryKeys`, `AccountKey=` or SAS connection string remains in the five modules' outputs or in `customer.bicep` outputs; `git grep -n "storageConnectionString\|serviceBusConnectionString\|searchServiceAdminKey\|openAiKey"` outside historical notes/CHANGELOG returns nothing.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`customer.json` contains role assignments for the L2 UAMI with Search Service Contributor and Search Index Data Contributor on the stamp search service, emitted only when `controlPlaneUamiPrincipalId` is non-empty; the BFF runtime UAMI grants are unchanged.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">`az bicep build` + lint clean; checked-in `customer.json` = fresh compile; `bicep-e2e-dry-run.ps1` PASS; ControlPlane.Tests no new failures; affected Pester suites pass.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">The consumer inventory (step 1) is recorded in the notes and every escalation trigger is answered (fired or not, with evidence).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Test scope: assertions for the four properties, the removed outputs and the two L2 roles; anything beyond needs a one-line justification in the notes.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    Filed 2026-10-06 (SESSION 37) from plan §7 T244 after T242b closed; facts in the background read the same day.
  

    COMPLETED 2026-10-06 (session 37). Template only — no live Azure change (T186 deploys it; T230 makes the runtime MI calls).

    STEP 1 CONSUMER INVENTORY (escalation triggers):
    - AI Search: BFF via MI (AiSearch__ManagedIdentity__Enabled, SearchClientFactory key-if-configured); L2 H2b
      (DefaultAzureCredential) + H13 tenant-filter probe (live /docs/search as L2) — L2 had NO Search role (G16).
    - OpenAI: stamp catalog carries only AzureOpenAI-Endpoint; OpenAiClient/AiModule use a key only if set. Stamp
      kind is OpenAI (E-2 was observed on dev's AIServices kind) — T230 measures it.
    - Document Intelligence: MI since T243; no stamp has a DocIntelKey setting.
    - Service Bus: BFF + membership publisher by namespace (ServiceBus__FullyQualifiedNamespace) + MI; the SAS rule
      fed only the template output.
    - Storage: BFF session blobs use endpoint + credential (stamp sets no SessionFileStore:BlobEndpoint today).
      Event Grid dead-letter (deployAcsMessaging) had no identity -> trigger 1 FIRED -> owner chose system-topic MI.
    - Cosmos: BFF CosmosClientBuilder(endpoint, credential) + UAMI sqlRoleAssignment -> owner added it to T244.
    - Template outputs: only legacy Provision-Customer.ps1 read storageConnectionString/serviceBusConnectionString
      (L2 no longer shells out to it). Rotate-Secrets.ps1 -Scope Customer minted Storage/SB keys into the customer
      vault (found by both reviews) -> retired as explicit no-ops. Dev-only scripts Add-ReferenceToIndex.ps1 /
      Sync-RecordsToIndex.ps1 list dev's OpenAI key (shared dev, not stamps — AC2 grep hit, accepted).
    - L2 handlers, sidecar: no key/SAS use. Trigger 2 did not fire; trigger 3 did not fire.

    DONE: disableLocalAuth true on AI Search (no authOptions), OpenAI, Document Intelligence, Service Bus, Cosmos
    (owner 2026-10-06); Storage shared key off (customer.bicep passes true; module default now true). Removed outputs
    searchServiceAdminKey/QueryKey, openAiKey, serviceBusConnectionString (+ SAS rule SpaarkeAppAccess), storage
    connectionString, customer storageConnectionString/serviceBusConnectionString. L2 UAMI: Search Service Contributor
    (H2b) + Search Index Data READER (H13 probe; L2 writes no documents — least privilege, deviation from the AC's
    "Index Data Contributor", reason recorded) on the stamp search service, conditional on the principal (Model 1).
    ACS Event Grid dead-letter: deadLetterWithResourceIdentity + system-topic SystemAssigned identity + Storage Blob
    Data Contributor on the dead-letter container. H2b: a provisioner 401/403 -> Resumable `search-access-denied`
    (role propagation after H2a; was Quarantine) + tests. Provision-Customer.ps1 no longer reads/writes the two
    connection strings. Rotate-Secrets.ps1 customer Storage/SB rotation retired (Rotate-StorageKey removed; Pester
    updated). Forcing function tests/Spaarke.ArchTests/CustomerStampKeylessTemplateTests.cs (11 facts: 5 real-template
    rules + controls; the 5 rules fail on the pre-T244 customer.json). Docs: inventory (incl. drift fix: stamp OpenAI is
    kind=OpenAI, not AIServices), deployment guide, provisioning.md keyless rule, azure-deployment.md Service Bus row,
    ADR-028 E-2 informational note, CHANGELOG.

    VERIFIED: ControlPlane.Tests 2118 pass / 0 fail / 1 skip; ArchTests 360/360 (11 new); Pester gates 27/27; bicep lint = master (only pre-existing
    warnings); customer.json = fresh compile; bicep-e2e-dry-run Build PASS (notes/bicep-e2e-dry-run-20261005.md).

    STEP 9.5: code-review (0 Critical; W1 H2b race FIXED; W2 Rotate-Secrets FIXED; W3 over-claim FIXED by adding Cosmos;
    S1-S9, S11 FIXED; S10 accepted above; S12 Model 2 Lighthouse would need both Search roles — Model 2 out of scope;
    S13 ACS local auth — documented exclusion; S14 dates are UTC). adr-check (0 hard violations; B-1 resolved by the
    owner's Cosmos decision (path C); W-1 E-2 note added; W-2/W-3 FIXED; W-4 FIXED; W-5 claim corrected; W-6 FIXED
    (Reader); W-7 comment; W-8 ADR-028 cited; W-9 accepted — single same-RG caller).

    FOLLOW-UPS: (1) CI check that the checked-in customer.json equals a fresh compile (the ArchTests read the
    checked-in JSON; CI publishes its own compile) — needs a pinned Bicep version to avoid templateHash noise;
    (2) T230 runtime MI call per service incl. E-2 measurement on kind=OpenAI; (3) ACS disableLocalAuth once its
    module API is raised.
  </notes>
</task>
